# Line endings are not cosmetic here.
#
# The memory sync compares file hashes to decide what changed. A file that differs only by
# a carriage return hashes differently, looks edited on both machines at once, and gets
# reported as a conflict - and a conflict deliberately keeps its old baseline, so nothing
# self-heals. That is how sync once stopped entirely. See docs/sync.md.
#
# So: normalize in the repository, and let checkout decide what each platform gets.
* text=auto

# PowerShell on Windows. CRLF on checkout, and never touched by an editor that guesses.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Documentation and vault content stay LF wherever they land, because these are the files
# the sync actually compares across machines.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
